WEBVTT

00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:12.650
He ain't like me...

00:00:12.650 --> 00:00:14.530
The importance of puzzles to him!

00:00:14.530 --> 00:00:17.300
Kaito, what the hell are you?

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:20.450
What do you want me to do?

00:00:24.710 --> 00:00:26.630
That's the time already?!

00:00:26.630 --> 00:00:28.650
I'm gonna be late!

00:00:30.340 --> 00:00:31.850
Big brother!

00:00:31.850 --> 00:00:34.760
You gotta eat a good breakfast, Miharu.

00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:36.890
You'll get anemic again.

00:00:37.710 --> 00:00:41.270
Sorry, brother, I made
you cook breakfast.

00:00:43.660 --> 00:00:45.640
Oh, that's right!

00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:49.860
I got a call from the editor of
Monthly Puzzle Prince yesterday!

00:00:49.880 --> 00:00:54.590
FullMetal Cube
Sudoku
Loop Courses
Matrix Logic

00:00:50.130 --> 00:00:54.610
The readers voted your puzzle
this month's No. 1 again!

00:00:54.790 --> 00:00:57.550
"Please, send in another one!" he said.

00:00:58.610 --> 00:01:00.660
I wanna tell all my friends about it:

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:03.510
Setsu Chido, the puzzle-maker who's

00:01:03.510 --> 00:01:06.390
all the rage, is really my brother!

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:08.610
I'm grateful.

00:01:08.610 --> 00:01:12.250
It's thanks to you that
the two of us can get by.

00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:14.610
Hurry up and eat.

00:01:14.990 --> 00:01:17.800
Still, you sure are great, brother.

00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:19.680
You're good at solving puzzles,

00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:22.690
but you're even better at making them!

00:01:24.290 --> 00:01:25.580
Better at making...

00:01:26.370 --> 00:01:27.900
than solving...

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:49.880
Kimi no nounai e to shinnyuu
Gonna infiltrate your brain

00:01:49.880 --> 00:01:52.670
Nemutteru suki ni baby, open the gate
While you're sleeping, baby, open the gate

00:01:52.670 --> 00:01:54.460
Fukuzatsusugi security
Too-complicated security

00:01:54.460 --> 00:01:57.220
Kakusareru to abakitakunaru
When something's hidden, it makes me want to expose it

00:01:57.220 --> 00:02:01.720
Barabara ni chirabatte iru password o hiroiatsume
I'll gather up those loose, scattered passwords

00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:06.430
Kakushin ni sematte yuku, sono shoutai o misete
And approach the core, so show me that true form

00:02:06.430 --> 00:02:08.640
Kantan ni clear dekinai
I can't clear it easily

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:11.310
Saki nante motto yomenai
Can read what lies ahead even less

00:02:11.310 --> 00:02:13.320
Kaidoku fukanou smile
A smile that can't be deciphered

00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:15.610
Kiken na puzzle
A dangerous puzzle

00:02:15.610 --> 00:02:17.570
Lock sareteta door aru nara
If there's a door that's been locked

00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:20.360
Zutto tataite miru beki, kaza-ana hiraku wa
You must keep striking it, a crack will open

00:02:20.360 --> 00:02:24.910
Eien ni hodokenai nazo nanka wa nai
No mystery remains unsolved forever

00:02:24.910 --> 00:02:27.160
Makiokosu, it's a supernova!
It's forming, it's a supernova!

00:02:27.160 --> 00:02:31.830
Tobikiri shigekiteki na hirameki o agemashou
I will give you thoroughly stimulating insight

00:02:31.830 --> 00:02:34.090
Misskey-misskey la-tu-ma

00:02:34.090 --> 00:02:36.420
Yume no naka, it's a supernova!
In the middle of a dream, it's a supernova!

00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:39.050
Watashi wa, sou, brain diver
I am, yes, a brain diver

00:02:39.050 --> 00:02:44.930
Kimi ga sagashimotometeru kotae ni nareru made
Until I become familiar with the answer you seek

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:50.600
Brain diver

00:02:52.350 --> 00:02:55.400
Brain diver

00:03:00.030 --> 00:03:03.990
Rebellion Against the Light

00:03:07.140 --> 00:03:09.250
The atmosphere on Genius Terrace...

00:03:09.250 --> 00:03:11.310
It's kinda strange, isn't it?

00:03:14.150 --> 00:03:15.480
Flap, flap!

00:03:17.890 --> 00:03:22.000
Ka - I - To!

00:03:23.070 --> 00:03:24.300
Flap, flap, flap, flap!

00:03:26.620 --> 00:03:29.900
It would have to be weird,
with a costume like that.

00:03:29.900 --> 00:03:31.780
What could she be thinking?

00:03:31.780 --> 00:03:33.060
Friggin' Itou.

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:37.690
There's that, but usually there are
five of them, and today...

00:03:38.020 --> 00:03:41.470
Well, you sure are ignoring me, Kaito.

00:03:41.470 --> 00:03:44.240
This outfit right in front of you...

00:03:45.450 --> 00:03:47.950
I guess I can understand, but...

00:03:49.110 --> 00:03:50.120
Good grief!

00:03:50.550 --> 00:03:53.730
This is when we most need a
Party to Cheer Up Kaito!

00:03:53.730 --> 00:03:56.710
I told them to get together in costume,

00:03:56.710 --> 00:03:59.160
so why is no one here?!

00:04:01.620 --> 00:04:03.300
What are you doing, Nonoha?!

00:04:05.240 --> 00:04:06.860
Sorry, sorry.

00:04:07.650 --> 00:04:11.360
So, you're thinking
of them? Your parents?

00:04:17.180 --> 00:04:18.650
It was a shock, huh?

00:04:19.420 --> 00:04:22.250
I never thought your mom and dad were...

00:04:23.030 --> 00:04:25.710
But you were happy, Kaito.

00:04:26.570 --> 00:04:30.240
The memories from that time aren't fake.

00:04:30.590 --> 00:04:33.920
They'll live on inside you, forever.

00:04:35.380 --> 00:04:36.800
I know that.

00:04:37.800 --> 00:04:41.070
I was thinking about Rook just now.

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:42.960
Rook?

00:04:43.580 --> 00:04:46.320
Yeah, he said he was separated from

00:04:46.320 --> 00:04:48.510
his parents when he was a kid too.

00:04:49.810 --> 00:04:52.820
But unlike me, he was all alone.

00:04:53.330 --> 00:04:55.650
In that damn, hideous room...

00:04:57.570 --> 00:04:58.720
They're devils.

00:05:00.290 --> 00:05:01.820
The POG!

00:05:02.250 --> 00:05:06.550
For you to worry about Rook,
after all he's done to you...

00:05:07.150 --> 00:05:09.120
You sure are tough, Kaito.

00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:10.620
You're an idiot, though.

00:05:10.620 --> 00:05:13.540
Hey! You didn't have to call me an idiot!

00:05:14.610 --> 00:05:16.560
<i>Mr. Kaito Daimon...</i>

00:05:16.560 --> 00:05:18.080
<i>Mr. Gammon Sakanoue...</i>

00:05:18.570 --> 00:05:20.570
<i>Mr. Cubik Galois...</i>

00:05:20.570 --> 00:05:21.890
<i>Mr. Ana Gram...</i>

00:05:22.540 --> 00:05:24.410
<i>Miss Nonoha Itou...</i>

00:05:24.410 --> 00:05:27.010
<i>Please come to the
principal's office at once.</i>

00:05:27.510 --> 00:05:28.620
That voice...

00:05:28.620 --> 00:05:30.420
It's the principal!

00:05:30.420 --> 00:05:32.590
That old fox is all right.

00:05:32.590 --> 00:05:33.710
Let's go, Nonoha!

00:05:35.570 --> 00:05:36.940
Change out of that.

00:05:36.940 --> 00:05:38.570
You look like a fool.

00:05:38.560 --> 00:05:40.430
You say that now?!

00:05:40.430 --> 00:05:41.690
Wait, a fool?!

00:05:42.550 --> 00:05:43.690
Hey, Pops!t

00:05:46.390 --> 00:05:48.320
Thank you for coming, Kaito.

00:05:50.320 --> 00:05:52.130
What the heck is this?

00:05:52.840 --> 00:05:57.180
I am Baron Kaidou,
principal of Root Gakuen High School.

00:05:57.180 --> 00:05:59.790
I'm a slightly mischievous Pisces.
Blood type: B.

00:06:00.330 --> 00:06:03.050
Upperclassman Jikukawa? What's that?

00:06:03.560 --> 00:06:04.860
A voice changer.

00:06:05.550 --> 00:06:08.130
Should something happen to me,

00:06:08.520 --> 00:06:10.500
Mr. Jikukawa would act
as my doppelganger,

00:06:10.500 --> 00:06:13.180
so as not to upset the students.

00:06:14.370 --> 00:06:17.600
I thought I'd let you all know.

00:06:18.110 --> 00:06:20.570
So, the principal is...

00:06:20.570 --> 00:06:22.400
He's still missing.

00:06:22.960 --> 00:06:24.430
But don't worry.

00:06:24.430 --> 00:06:28.280
He's a tough old bird,
anything but ordinary.

00:06:28.590 --> 00:06:30.550
I'm sure he's okay.

00:06:31.020 --> 00:06:31.810
Yeah...

00:06:32.520 --> 00:06:33.840
Yeah, you're right.

00:06:33.840 --> 00:06:35.540
Yup, I think so.

00:06:35.870 --> 00:06:38.830
Well, his doppelganger has it tough, too.

00:06:39.190 --> 00:06:40.810
Don't worry.

00:06:40.810 --> 00:06:44.080
There's no way I'm gonna lose to the POG.

00:06:44.080 --> 00:06:45.090
That's right!

00:06:45.560 --> 00:06:47.680
If we all join forces...

00:06:47.680 --> 00:06:48.630
Huh?

00:06:49.220 --> 00:06:51.480
Speaking of, where are
Gammon and the others?

00:06:51.950 --> 00:06:53.540
That's right.

00:06:53.540 --> 00:06:56.640
I haven't seen the three of them today.

00:06:57.000 --> 00:06:59.670
It's like they're avoiding us.

00:07:00.520 --> 00:07:01.660
Avoiding...

00:07:02.020 --> 00:07:03.810
So, the time has come.

00:07:08.260 --> 00:07:10.330
Oh, Mr. Genius!

00:07:10.330 --> 00:07:12.410
You give up on the third problem?

00:07:12.600 --> 00:07:14.560
I'm so sad!

00:07:14.560 --> 00:07:16.540
Don't go givin' Erena problems!

00:07:18.540 --> 00:07:20.940
I thought you were the
friggin' Puzzle King!

00:07:20.940 --> 00:07:22.310
Cut the crap!

00:07:22.310 --> 00:07:23.710
Solve it already!

00:07:23.710 --> 00:07:25.430
Please, sir.

00:07:25.430 --> 00:07:27.590
Don't let something bad happen to me.

00:07:27.610 --> 00:07:30.170
Y..Yes, but still...

00:07:31.420 --> 00:07:33.290
I'm so cute, and yet...

00:07:33.290 --> 00:07:35.950
Oh, how naughty I am!

00:07:37.500 --> 00:07:39.770
No! Don't cry!

00:07:40.170 --> 00:07:45.400
Kind sirs, please forgive
wicked little Erena-poo.

00:07:45.560 --> 00:07:47.730
We forgive you-poo!

00:07:48.170 --> 00:07:50.130
P..Poo!

00:07:51.010 --> 00:07:53.740
Oh! Erena-poo wins!

00:08:02.200 --> 00:08:04.510
What's this turn of events?

00:08:04.510 --> 00:08:07.670
Why did you come watch my show?

00:08:07.960 --> 00:08:09.800
You've changed your shtick again.

00:08:10.550 --> 00:08:11.910
And that's bad?

00:08:11.910 --> 00:08:14.070
The high-and-mighty queen act is old.

00:08:14.070 --> 00:08:16.450
In the cutthroat entertainment industry,

00:08:16.450 --> 00:08:17.390
it's to be expected.

00:08:18.920 --> 00:08:21.350
Seeing that damn self-satisfied
look of yours again

00:08:21.350 --> 00:08:22.660
has made me feel better.

00:08:23.520 --> 00:08:24.870
You're a bit strange.

00:08:25.820 --> 00:08:27.790
Is something bugging you?

00:08:29.530 --> 00:08:30.570
Bull's eye?

00:08:30.570 --> 00:08:31.990
Shut yer yap!

00:08:31.990 --> 00:08:32.650
See ya.

00:08:33.550 --> 00:08:36.880
Wait, Mr. Puzzlemaker, Setsu Chido!

00:08:38.530 --> 00:08:39.660
You...

00:08:40.170 --> 00:08:40.830
How do you...

00:08:41.210 --> 00:08:43.790
Don't underestimate the
POG information net.

00:08:44.420 --> 00:08:46.020
It happen sometimes:

00:08:46.020 --> 00:08:50.510
Someone is skilled at being
both a Giver and a Solver.

00:08:50.510 --> 00:08:52.660
Is that what's bugging you?

00:08:53.440 --> 00:08:54.800
What're you tryin' to say?

00:08:55.130 --> 00:08:56.640
Do you want to get some coffee?

00:08:57.120 --> 00:08:59.560
Genius Giver, Mr. Chido?

00:09:02.120 --> 00:09:06.830
Cube, why didn't you come at noon?

00:09:06.830 --> 00:09:08.730
Anyway, come out!

00:09:09.090 --> 00:09:11.360
Open the door! Open it!

00:09:11.360 --> 00:09:12.720
Cube?

00:09:12.030 --> 00:09:13.640
It won't reach him.

00:09:12.720 --> 00:09:14.860
You're in there, aren't you?

00:09:13.640 --> 00:09:14.860
Kaito...

00:09:15.500 --> 00:09:17.530
You want to devote yourself to painting?

00:09:18.250 --> 00:09:21.790
Ana, the two of you are acting weird.

00:09:21.790 --> 00:09:24.500
It's like you're avoiding Kaito and me.

00:09:26.350 --> 00:09:28.070
I, Ana, think...

00:09:28.070 --> 00:09:32.300
The sun has chased the
moon and gone far away.

00:09:32.710 --> 00:09:35.300
The sun? Kaito?

00:09:36.230 --> 00:09:39.060
The path has grown dark,
and I, Ana, can't follow.

00:09:39.060 --> 00:09:39.960
Ana...

00:09:41.170 --> 00:09:42.520
I...

00:09:42.520 --> 00:09:44.390
I will follow!

00:09:44.800 --> 00:09:46.170
No matter where!

00:09:46.170 --> 00:09:47.770
No matter how far!

00:09:58.130 --> 00:09:59.300
Master Rook...

00:10:00.230 --> 00:10:02.660
Are you somewhat tired?

00:10:03.020 --> 00:10:05.370
Me? Why?

00:10:05.370 --> 00:10:07.020
Oh, no reason.

00:10:07.410 --> 00:10:09.170
Continue with your report.

00:10:10.300 --> 00:10:11.280
Sir.

00:10:11.280 --> 00:10:13.760
Our prior plan has borne fruit.

00:10:13.760 --> 00:10:17.220
Edison/Cubik Galois and Da Vinci/Ana Gram

00:10:17.510 --> 00:10:20.180
have begun to distance themselves
from Kaito Daimon.

00:10:20.660 --> 00:10:21.940
Okay!

00:10:21.940 --> 00:10:24.450
Next up is my puzzle.

00:10:24.450 --> 00:10:26.900
If we kill his companions all at once,

00:10:26.900 --> 00:10:29.940
Kaito Daimon will be completely alone!

00:10:30.390 --> 00:10:32.020
I don't know about that.

00:10:32.720 --> 00:10:36.190
If we killed them, they
would live on forever.

00:10:36.770 --> 00:10:40.110
Having them alive will serve
to deepen Kaito's solitude.

00:10:40.110 --> 00:10:43.030
Yeah, I don't follow that.

00:10:44.280 --> 00:10:46.190
These are the remaining two.

00:10:46.190 --> 00:10:48.540
Putting aside Nonoha Itou,

00:10:48.440 --> 00:10:51.060
Galileo/Gammon Sakanoue is...

00:10:51.060 --> 00:10:53.650
No, she is the problem.

00:10:54.220 --> 00:10:58.380
She is the greater of Kaito's
psychological supports.

00:10:58.700 --> 00:11:02.140
Galileo, by comparison, will be easy.

00:11:03.260 --> 00:11:05.160
As you foresaw, Master Rook,

00:11:05.160 --> 00:11:09.750
Gammon Sakanoue currently
seems quite shaken.

00:11:14.420 --> 00:11:18.300
I know his thoughts as well as my own.

00:11:19.040 --> 00:11:20.000
Kaito...

00:11:20.810 --> 00:11:23.030
This all rests on your reply.

00:11:33.780 --> 00:11:36.940
That's meant to be the school principal.

00:11:37.380 --> 00:11:40.080
And? What did you wanna tell me?

00:11:40.080 --> 00:11:41.750
The atmosphere here has worsened

00:11:41.750 --> 00:11:44.260
dramatically in the past few days.

00:11:44.930 --> 00:11:46.590
The principal disappeared,

00:11:46.590 --> 00:11:50.020
and with the POG's eyes on me,
I can't act out of turn.

00:11:50.500 --> 00:11:53.380
Gammon, what will you do next?

00:11:53.380 --> 00:11:54.880
Beats me.

00:11:54.880 --> 00:11:57.520
I'm at the age where I've got
plenty of problems of my own.

00:11:58.010 --> 00:11:59.980
I'll take an hour or
so to think about it.

00:12:00.530 --> 00:12:02.400
I'm counting on you.

00:12:02.400 --> 00:12:04.630
Just as the POG anticipated,

00:12:04.630 --> 00:12:07.590
Kaito is becoming more isolated.

00:12:08.650 --> 00:12:10.840
Nonoha will stick with him.

00:12:10.840 --> 00:12:12.620
No matter what, she'll follow Kaito.

00:12:12.620 --> 00:12:14.260
Nonoha?

00:12:15.460 --> 00:12:16.960
Nonoha's a non-issue.

00:12:17.720 --> 00:12:19.940
She has no skill with puzzles,

00:12:19.940 --> 00:12:22.370
so I'm sure the POG isn't interested in her.

00:12:25.490 --> 00:12:27.280
The Puzzle of God...

00:12:27.280 --> 00:12:28.600
The Book of God...

00:12:29.290 --> 00:12:32.370
The POG won't rule anything out
to solve the Puzzle of God

00:12:32.370 --> 00:12:36.110
and obtain the Book of God.

00:12:36.330 --> 00:12:38.410
Yeah, true enough.

00:12:38.410 --> 00:12:41.060
I'm sure money ain't an issue, either.

00:12:44.830 --> 00:12:45.860
Nonoha...

00:12:46.320 --> 00:12:47.870
Is something the matter?

00:12:47.870 --> 00:12:50.280
Well, what should I have for dinner?

00:12:56.640 --> 00:12:58.580
Th..This is...

00:12:58.580 --> 00:13:01.950
Such a beautiful, sophisticated sudoku!

00:13:01.950 --> 00:13:03.920
Gammon did this?

00:13:05.250 --> 00:13:09.130
Gammon, just what are you?

00:13:11.360 --> 00:13:14.350
So, both Ana and Cube are...

00:13:14.350 --> 00:13:17.520
At this rate, Kaito
will end up all alone.

00:13:18.520 --> 00:13:22.270
So, Gammon, stay Kaito's friend!

00:13:22.840 --> 00:13:25.570
Just like you've been
doing, you and Kaito...

00:13:28.320 --> 00:13:30.390
Kaito, why are you here?

00:13:30.390 --> 00:13:32.710
What gives? Nonoha's with you?

00:13:32.710 --> 00:13:34.080
I called him.

00:13:40.880 --> 00:13:42.250
So, what the hell?

00:13:42.250 --> 00:13:44.500
Sayin' you need me for something...

00:13:45.380 --> 00:13:48.470
I won't say this again, so listen up.

00:13:49.660 --> 00:13:52.470
I gotta prepare myself for
how you're gonna answer.

00:13:52.710 --> 00:13:53.700
Kaito...

00:13:54.590 --> 00:13:56.720
Don't go near Nonoha again.

00:13:57.320 --> 00:14:00.060
If you do, I'll knock your block off!

00:14:01.030 --> 00:14:01.980
Gammon!

00:14:06.200 --> 00:14:07.550
What a joke.

00:14:07.550 --> 00:14:09.490
I wondered what you were gonna say.

00:14:09.490 --> 00:14:11.200
You're an idiot, aren't you?

00:14:11.200 --> 00:14:14.990
You can't say something like
that, orderin' me around!

00:14:16.430 --> 00:14:18.120
So, that's your answer?

00:14:18.500 --> 00:14:20.350
And what if it is?

00:14:20.350 --> 00:14:22.860
Kaito, what's happened to

00:14:22.860 --> 00:14:24.750
Ana and Cubik since they met you?

00:14:30.360 --> 00:14:31.680
Well?!

00:14:32.170 --> 00:14:34.820
That's how you are, bastard!

00:14:35.350 --> 00:14:38.540
You're a self-important,
puzzle-obsessed fool

00:14:38.540 --> 00:14:40.630
who don't think about his friends at all!

00:14:41.280 --> 00:14:43.360
You're a brat who's happy bein'

00:14:43.360 --> 00:14:45.200
the only one playin' puzzles!

00:14:45.200 --> 00:14:47.500
H..Hey, Gammon!

00:14:47.500 --> 00:14:49.480
That's going too far.

00:14:49.480 --> 00:14:50.200
Nonoha!

00:14:51.010 --> 00:14:53.240
Kaito's gonna get you killed!

00:14:54.940 --> 00:14:57.310
When the Armlet of Orpheus takes over,

00:14:57.310 --> 00:15:00.080
Kaito will lose himself
and leave you for dead!

00:15:00.990 --> 00:15:03.450
Kaito is a plague, bringin'

00:15:03.450 --> 00:15:05.080
misfortune to those around him!

00:15:05.080 --> 00:15:07.090
A..A plague?

00:15:07.670 --> 00:15:11.300
That's why you can't have
nothin' to do with Kaito, ever!

00:15:11.920 --> 00:15:13.390
Mind your own business.

00:15:14.420 --> 00:15:16.920
I'll decide what's best for me!

00:15:16.920 --> 00:15:18.770
I'll do as I like!

00:15:19.230 --> 00:15:21.150
You're a disappointment, Gammon.

00:15:26.840 --> 00:15:28.140
Oh, is that so?

00:15:28.630 --> 00:15:30.510
Then that settles it.

00:15:30.510 --> 00:15:32.910
Going forward, I'll do as I like, too.

00:15:33.650 --> 00:15:35.650
I finally get it.

00:15:36.230 --> 00:15:38.960
I know what you are to me.

00:15:38.960 --> 00:15:40.140
You're an enemy.

00:15:40.140 --> 00:15:42.160
An enemy I have to crush!

00:15:43.030 --> 00:15:45.670
Kaito Daimon, fight me!

00:15:46.760 --> 00:15:49.120
Challenge the puzzle that I've made!

00:15:49.120 --> 00:15:49.920
Gammon!

00:15:53.680 --> 00:15:57.770
You're idiots! Both of you!

00:16:06.170 --> 00:16:07.380
What's this?

00:16:12.640 --> 00:16:15.200
Did Gammon really make this?

00:16:15.410 --> 00:16:16.200
Use the 4 pieces
to make a "T"!!

00:16:16.410 --> 00:16:17.200
Connect the 9 dots using
4 continuous lines!!

00:16:17.410 --> 00:16:18.200
What numbers go in A and B?!

00:16:18.320 --> 00:16:21.100
Those hand-drawn puzzles...

00:16:21.100 --> 00:16:21.960
That was you, too?

00:16:22.480 --> 00:16:23.690
That's right.

00:16:23.690 --> 00:16:28.210
My talent is first-rate,
as a Solver and a Giver!

00:16:28.660 --> 00:16:29.900
I'm the true genius,

00:16:29.900 --> 00:16:33.050
one that your dumb ass ain't close to!

00:16:33.830 --> 00:16:35.410
Now you're talkin' nonsense.

00:16:35.410 --> 00:16:37.470
There's no puzzle I can't solve!

00:16:39.310 --> 00:16:42.600
Look, why has it come to this?

00:16:42.600 --> 00:16:44.730
The two of you are real idiots!

00:16:45.330 --> 00:16:47.590
This is an opposition-style puzzle.

00:16:50.550 --> 00:16:51.870
There are nine rows and

00:16:51.870 --> 00:16:54.860
nine columns of poles,
eighty-one in total.

00:16:54.860 --> 00:16:57.950
The ones at either corner
are the "mother poles."

00:16:59.300 --> 00:17:01.510
If you strike two poles,

00:17:01.510 --> 00:17:03.660
it creates a laser barrier between them.

00:17:04.440 --> 00:17:07.280
You can make eight barriers at once.

00:17:07.280 --> 00:17:09.490
Make barriers to form an enclosure,

00:17:09.490 --> 00:17:11.840
including the mother pole to start.

00:17:11.840 --> 00:17:13.630
If you don't make an enclosure,
they'll disappear.

00:17:14.290 --> 00:17:16.270
Each person can only make one enclosure,

00:17:16.270 --> 00:17:20.410
but you can expand it or cut
it off to make it smaller.

00:17:20.830 --> 00:17:22.770
We can also use the same poles to

00:17:22.770 --> 00:17:25.380
make two-layered barriers.

00:17:25.380 --> 00:17:27.820
Whoever gets their
opponent into a dead end

00:17:27.820 --> 00:17:30.150
and surrounds them on four sides wins.

00:17:32.010 --> 00:17:33.190
All right.

00:17:46.000 --> 00:17:48.330
Puzzle time, let's begin.

00:17:49.750 --> 00:17:50.960
Here I come!

00:17:50.960 --> 00:17:53.630
There's no order, no turns!
The fastest one wins!

00:17:53.830 --> 00:17:55.630
Now you tell me!

00:17:57.220 --> 00:17:58.220
No way!

00:17:58.220 --> 00:17:59.390
If the faster person wins,

00:17:59.390 --> 00:18:01.010
then Gammon has the advantage

00:18:01.010 --> 00:18:02.750
because he made the puzzle!

00:18:03.060 --> 00:18:04.630
That ain't so!

00:18:13.570 --> 00:18:15.280
Forget it!

00:18:21.950 --> 00:18:24.740
They're both fighting for real.

00:18:24.740 --> 00:18:25.870
Why?

00:18:32.220 --> 00:18:33.580
This is fun.

00:18:33.580 --> 00:18:34.760
This is a good puzzle!

00:18:35.240 --> 00:18:38.010
You sure are great, Gammon!

00:18:38.010 --> 00:18:41.200
I forgot to mention one thing:

00:18:41.200 --> 00:18:43.610
If you get forced into a dead end

00:18:43.610 --> 00:18:45.270
and you're gonna lose...

00:18:50.710 --> 00:18:53.020
I..It blows up? Why?!

00:18:53.990 --> 00:18:55.200
I told you, didn't I?

00:18:55.690 --> 00:18:57.280
It's a "dead" end!

00:18:57.290 --> 00:18:58.450
Gammon!

00:19:06.230 --> 00:19:08.040
Stop it, Gammon!

00:19:08.030 --> 00:19:09.180
Not this...

00:19:09.770 --> 00:19:10.960
Not this kind of puzzle!

00:19:11.270 --> 00:19:12.460
I can't stop.

00:19:12.930 --> 00:19:15.160
Not till I crush you!

00:19:18.670 --> 00:19:19.770
Gammon!

00:19:21.260 --> 00:19:22.820
Drop dead, Kaito!

00:19:22.820 --> 00:19:24.560
Die in this Puzzle of Fools!

00:19:25.680 --> 00:19:27.810
What? A Puzzle of Fools?

00:19:28.180 --> 00:19:29.310
That's right!

00:19:29.300 --> 00:19:34.380
This is a Puzzle of Fools
I made just for you!

00:19:35.650 --> 00:19:37.210
What's the matter?!

00:19:37.210 --> 00:19:39.690
You're the most gifted
Phi-Brain candidate!

00:19:39.690 --> 00:19:41.950
You get scared and lose your nerve?!

00:19:51.210 --> 00:19:52.240
Gammon...

00:19:52.920 --> 00:19:53.790
Bastard!

00:19:54.690 --> 00:19:57.380
Go to Hell, Kaito.

00:19:57.930 --> 00:19:59.260
I've had it.

00:19:59.260 --> 00:20:02.550
I'm gonna smash this
piece-of-shit puzzle of yours!

00:20:03.200 --> 00:20:05.200
That has a hollow ring to it.

00:20:05.200 --> 00:20:06.890
You think you can win?!

00:20:12.270 --> 00:20:15.180
Use your armlet, Kaito!

00:20:15.180 --> 00:20:18.650
Rely on the armlet like you always do!

00:20:19.080 --> 00:20:20.320
Shut up!

00:20:26.220 --> 00:20:27.200
What?!

00:20:38.020 --> 00:20:38.920
Oh, no!

00:20:43.560 --> 00:20:45.590
You lost your cool and
missed the final blow, huh?

00:20:48.230 --> 00:20:50.450
Fine, finish me off.

00:20:51.210 --> 00:20:53.060
If you don't, you won't have won!

00:20:54.230 --> 00:20:57.310
When the armlet takes you,
you've got no emotions!

00:20:57.480 --> 00:20:58.610
You can do it, can't you?

00:20:59.250 --> 00:21:00.900
Do it, dammit.

00:21:00.900 --> 00:21:01.900
Do it!

00:21:01.900 --> 00:21:04.200
No! Kaito!

00:21:18.210 --> 00:21:22.820
I'm gonna make you regret
showin' me mercy,

00:21:23.510 --> 00:21:26.140
Einstein... Kaito Daimon!

00:21:28.550 --> 00:21:29.640
Gammon!

00:21:30.250 --> 00:21:33.060
Why did he do this?

00:21:36.830 --> 00:21:37.690
Kaito?

00:21:46.230 --> 00:21:47.460
Kaito...

00:21:50.220 --> 00:21:54.080
Sure enough, my cooking is
a weapon of destruction.

00:21:54.630 --> 00:21:56.560
I'm so hungry!

00:21:56.560 --> 00:21:59.710
Hurry up and come home, brother!

00:22:01.810 --> 00:22:04.010
You really fought him.

00:22:04.790 --> 00:22:07.710
I'm surprised, that's kind of a big deal.

00:22:08.620 --> 00:22:09.800
You're fine with this?

00:22:10.430 --> 00:22:11.590
No regrets?

00:22:12.040 --> 00:22:15.310
I ain't never had one, a regret.

00:22:19.970 --> 00:22:23.820
To crush Kaito Daimon, I...

00:22:25.150 --> 00:22:27.750
I'll become a POG Giver.

00:22:37.240 --> 00:22:41.540
Tsukue no ue de umareta sekai
A world born on top of a desk

00:22:41.540 --> 00:22:47.340
Ichiban saki ni kimi ni misetakatta
I wanted to show it to you first of all

00:22:47.770 --> 00:22:52.090
Karappo no heya sotto nukedashite
I sneaked silently out of that empty room

00:22:52.090 --> 00:22:57.210
Hashirihajimeteta
And started running

00:22:58.290 --> 00:23:02.610
Iki hazumasete oka o noboru to
Breathing heavily, I climbed the hill

00:23:02.610 --> 00:23:08.220
Kimi ga saki ni tsuite matte ita ne
And you were already there, waiting

00:23:08.900 --> 00:23:13.160
Takusan no hajimete kimi to mitsuketa
There were so many treasures that I first

00:23:13.160 --> 00:23:17.910
Takaramono datta
Discovered with you

00:23:18.410 --> 00:23:24.020
Kanashisa de afureta toki wa
That time when I was overcome with sadness

00:23:24.020 --> 00:23:26.600
Nanimo iwazu ni tada
You said nothing

00:23:26.600 --> 00:23:29.250
Soba ni ite kureta ne
Just stayed there by my side, didn't you?

00:23:29.250 --> 00:23:33.910
Imademo wasurenai yo
Even now, I haven't forgotten

00:23:33.910 --> 00:23:39.180
Mata aou ne, yakusoku o shiyou
Let's meet again, let's make it a promise

00:23:39.180 --> 00:23:44.400
Kei wa shinai, ano hi no sayonara
It won't fade, the "goodbye" of that day

00:23:44.400 --> 00:23:50.050
Boku no subete, kimi ga kureta michi
Everything I have, the path you gave me

00:23:50.050 --> 00:23:58.960
Zutto kokoro no naka hikaru yo
Will always shine within my heart

00:24:02.920 --> 00:24:05.220
Will ya let me join the POG?

00:24:05.220 --> 00:24:06.320
Why not?

00:24:06.320 --> 00:24:08.760
First, let's have you clean my room.

00:24:08.760 --> 00:24:10.420
Clean?

00:24:10.420 --> 00:24:11.870
After that, do the grounds.

00:24:11.870 --> 00:24:14.490
And then one hundred pushups and sit-ups.

00:24:14.490 --> 00:24:16.240
Hmph! Gimme a break!

00:24:16.240 --> 00:24:19.140
Puzzles require physical strength.

00:24:19.670 --> 00:24:21.980
Next time, "The Proof of Betrayal"

00:24:19.950 --> 00:24:27.550
The Proof of Betrayal

00:24:22.230 --> 00:24:25.730
Can I make it here?
